---
import { getCollection } from 'astro:content';
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import IntroActions from '../components/IntroActions.astro';
import PageShortcuts from '../components/PageShortcuts.astro';
import Section from '../components/Section.astro';
import Papers from '../components/Papers.astro';
import ResearchAreas from '../components/ResearchAreas.astro';
import Disclosure from '../components/Disclosure.astro';
import SectionLinks from '../components/SectionLinks.astro';
import { researchAgenda } from '../data/institute';
import { groups } from '../data/groups';
import { external } from '../lib/external';
const featuredGroupId = 'game-theoretic-foundations';
const orderedGroups = [...groups.filter((g) => g.id === featuredGroupId), ...groups.filter((g) => g.id !== featuredGroupId)];
const papers = (await getCollection('selectedResearch')).sort(
  (a, b) => a.data.order - b.data.order,
);
---

<Base
  title="Research"
  description="RESI's research outputs, research questions, AI-assisted methods, working groups, and prior research by its community."
>
  <Section id="thesis" class="landing">
    <h1 class="page-title">How can we formally define and implement AI safety?</h1>
    <p>
      RESI focuses on the formal and design-oriented foundations of AI safety: precise safety
      objectives, explicit assumptions, mechanisms with analyzable guarantees, composition, and
      impossibility results.
    </p>
    <p>
      Guarantees depend on stated assumptions about the system and adversary. They do not establish
      the safety of an entire AI system.
    </p>
    <p>
      <strong>Our goal is to build approaches that develop together with systems as they become superintelligent.</strong>
    </p>
    <p id="ai-assisted">
      Research at RESI is AI-assisted from the start, with AI-generated suggestions subject to independent
      examination and testing. We will develop and continually improve tools and workflows that use frontier
      AI agents at every stage, expanding the ideas and approaches our team can investigate.
    </p>
    <IntroActions
      items={[
        { label: 'Meet the team', href: '/people' },
        { label: 'Support our work', href: '/support' },
      ]}
    />
  </Section>
  <PageShortcuts
    id="research-shortcuts"
    items={[
      { label: 'Research outputs', href: '#approach' },
      { label: 'Research areas', href: '#areas' },
      { label: 'Working groups', href: '#concentration' },
      { label: 'Foundational research', href: '#evidence' },
    ]}
  />



  <Section label="Research outputs" id="approach" divider>
    <p>Across our <a href="#areas">research areas</a>, we pursue the following outputs:</p>
    <ul class="research-outputs">
      <li class="research-output" id="define">
        <h3>Models, definitions, and impossibility results</h3>
        <div class="research-output-description">
          <p>Develop models and precise definitions for AI safety.</p>
          <p id="establish-limits">
            Establish where guarantees are impossible under stated assumptions.
          </p>
        </div>
      </li>
      <li class="research-output" id="build">
        <h3>Mechanisms and composition</h3>
        <div class="research-output-description">
          <p>
            Develop mechanisms, protocols, and architectures that provide useful guarantees, and study
            whether those guarantees survive composition into larger systems involving models, tools,
            people, and institutions.
          </p>
        </div>
      </li>
      <li class="research-output" id="implement">
        <h3>Implementations and proofs of concept</h3>
        <div class="research-output-description">
          <p>
            Build implementations and proofs of concept. Where implementation requires resources
            beyond RESI’s capacity, share proofs of concept that frontier AI developers can evaluate
            and adopt.
          </p>
        </div>
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p class="research-outputs-note">
      Definitions and constructions develop together: a new protocol may reveal the right concept,
      and an impossibility result may show that a problem must be reformulated.
    </p>
  </Section>

  <Section id="areas" divider>
    <div id="priorities">
      <h2 class="section-title">{researchAgenda.title}</h2>
      {researchAgenda.intro && <p>{researchAgenda.intro}</p>}
    </div>
    <p>
      These questions describe our key focus areas. In each area we pursue <a href="#approach">clear outputs</a> that include definitions, mechanisms,
      working demonstrations, and results on what can and cannot be guaranteed.
    </p>
    <ResearchAreas expanded />
  </Section>

  <!-- Keep #concentration for existing links and support #working on the heading. -->
  <Section label="Working groups" labelId="working" id="concentration" divider>
    <p>
      Working groups bring RESI researchers together to develop <a href="#approach">research outputs</a> across our <a href="#areas">key research areas</a>. They open new directions and revisit classical questions in light of
      superintelligence. Each group is organized by one or more leaders who decide on its structure.
      Alongside working groups, RESI co-hosts <a href="/seminars/">seminars</a> with MIT on the foundations of AI safety.
    </p>
    <ul class="group-list research-group-cards">
      {orderedGroups.map((g) => (
        <li class:list={["working-group", { "working-group-featured": g.id === featuredGroupId }]}>
          <h3 id={g.id}>{g.name}</h3>
          <div class="working-group-body">
          {g.lead && (
            <p class="wg-lead">
              Led by{' '}
              {g.leadHref ? (
                <a href={g.leadHref} {...external(g.leadHref)}>
                  {g.lead}
                </a>
              ) : (
                g.lead
              )}
            </p>
          )}
          <Disclosure summary="details" class="working-group-details" compactControl accessibleLabel={`${g.name}: details`}>
            {g.description && <p class="wg-description">{g.description}</p>}
            {g.source && (
              <p class="wg-source">
                <a href={g.source} {...external(g.source)}>
                  Read the announcement on LessWrong
                </a>
              </p>
            )}
            {(g.placement || g.relatedPaperAnchors) && (
              <p class="wg-source">
                {g.relatedPaperAnchors ? 'Related foundational research:' : 'Foundational research:'}{' '}
                {papers
                  .filter((p) => g.relatedPaperAnchors
                    ? g.relatedPaperAnchors.includes(p.data.anchor ?? '')
                    : p.data.placement === g.placement)
                  .map((p, i) => (
                    <Fragment>
                      {i > 0 && ' · '}
                      <a href={'#' + p.data.anchor}>{p.data.title}</a>
                    </Fragment>
                  ))}
              </p>
            )}
          </Disclosure>
          </div>
        </li>
      ))}
    </ul>
    <div class="working-group-onward">
      <SectionLinks align="end" emphasis items={[{ label: 'Meet the team', href: '/people' }]} />
    </div>
  </Section>

  <Section
    label="Foundational research by the RESI team"
    id="evidence"
    class="research-publications"
    divider
  >
    <p class="caption provenance">
      The papers below are prior work by researchers now associated with RESI.
    </p>
    <Papers
      showAttribution={false}
      placement={[
        'verification',
        'control',
        'limits',
        'cryptography',
        'wg-game-theoretic-foundations',
        'wg-legal-alignment',
        'wg-data-attribution',
      ]}
    />
  </Section>

  <script>
    // Keep the authored row-wise order for keyboard users and mobile while
    // letting each desktop column grow independently. Without JS, use the grid.
    const roster = document.querySelector<HTMLElement>('.research-group-cards');
    if (roster) {
      const allCards = [...roster.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>(':scope > .working-group')];
      const featured = roster.querySelector<HTMLElement>(':scope > .working-group-featured');
      const cards = allCards.filter((card) => card !== featured);
      const desktop = matchMedia('(min-width: 525.75px)');
      let scheduled = false;
      const layout = () => {
        scheduled = false;
        roster.style.removeProperty('--group-title-height');
        roster.style.removeProperty('--group-lead-height');
        if (!desktop.matches) {
          roster.classList.remove('independent-columns');
          allCards.forEach((card) => {
            card.style.removeProperty('grid-row');
            card.style.removeProperty('grid-column');
          });
          return;
        }
        roster.classList.add('independent-columns');
        // Match the closed-card headers at the current width, even while a
        // description is open. Expanded bodies still grow independently.
        const tallest = (selector: string) => Math.ceil(Math.max(...cards.map((card) =>
          card.querySelector<HTMLElement>(selector)?.getBoundingClientRect().height ?? 0
        )));
        const titleHeight = tallest(':scope > h3');
        const leadHeight = tallest(':scope > .working-group-body > .wg-lead');
        roster.style.setProperty('--group-title-height', `${titleHeight}px`);
        roster.style.setProperty('--group-lead-height', `${leadHeight}px`);
        const gap = Math.ceil(parseFloat(getComputedStyle(roster).columnGap));
        let firstRow = 1;
        if (featured) {
          featured.style.gridColumn = '1 / -1';
          const rows = Math.ceil(featured.getBoundingClientRect().height);
          featured.style.gridRow = `1 / span ${rows}`;
          firstRow += rows + gap;
        }
        const nextRow = [firstRow, firstRow];
        cards.forEach((card, index) => {
          const column = index % 2;
          const rows = Math.ceil(card.getBoundingClientRect().height);
          card.style.gridColumn = String(column + 1);
          card.style.gridRow = `${nextRow[column]} / span ${rows}`;
          nextRow[column] += rows + gap;
        });
      };
      const schedule = () => {
        if (!scheduled) {
          scheduled = true;
          requestAnimationFrame(layout);
        }
      };
      const observer = new ResizeObserver(schedule);
      allCards.forEach((card) => observer.observe(card));
      desktop.addEventListener('change', schedule);
      document.fonts.ready.then(schedule);
      layout();
    }
  </script>
</Base>

<style is:global>
  /* Three complementary outputs, presented as one editorial list. */
  #approach .research-outputs {
    display: block;
    list-style: none;
    padding: 0;
    margin: 30px 0 0;
  }
  #approach .research-output {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 0.9fr) minmax(0, 1.6fr);
    gap: 27px;
    padding: 19.5px 0;
    margin: 0;
    border-bottom: 0.75px solid var(--line);
  }
  #approach .research-output:first-child {
    padding-top: 0;
  }
  #approach .research-output h3 {
    margin: 0;
    font-size: 16.5px;
    line-height: 1.35;
    text-wrap: balance;
  }
  #approach .research-output-description p {
    margin: 0;
  }
  #approach .research-output-description p + p {
    margin-top: 6px;
  }
  #approach .research-output:last-child {
    border-bottom: 0;
    padding-bottom: 0;
  }
  #approach .research-outputs-note {
    margin: 30px 0 0;
  }
  @media (max-width: 525px) {
    #approach .research-output {
      grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr);
      gap: 7.5px;
      padding-block: 18px;
    }
  }

  .research-group-cards {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
    gap: 12px;
  }
  .research-group-cards > .working-group-featured {
    grid-column: 1 / -1;
  }
  @media screen and (min-width: 525.75px) {
    .research-group-cards > .working-group:not(.working-group-featured) > h3 {
      min-height: var(--group-title-height, 0px);
    }
    .research-group-cards > .working-group:not(.working-group-featured) > .working-group-body > .wg-lead {
      min-height: var(--group-lead-height, 0px);
    }
    .research-group-cards.independent-columns {
      /* The layout script measures row spans in whole CSS pixels. */
      grid-auto-rows: 1px;
      row-gap: 0;
    }
  }
  .research-group-cards > .working-group {
    min-width: 0;
    padding: 16.5px;
    border: 0.75px solid var(--line);
    border-radius: 2.25px;
    background: transparent;
    break-inside: avoid;
  }
  .research-group-cards > .working-group {
    display: block;
    margin: 0;
    padding: 13.5px 13.5px 7.5px;
  }
  .research-group-cards > .working-group > h3 {
    margin: 0;
  }
  .research-group-cards > .working-group > :last-child {
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }
  .research-group-cards {
    align-items: start;
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }
  .working-group-body {
    position: relative;
    min-height: 33px;
    padding-top: 6px;
  }
  .research-group-cards .wg-lead {
    margin: 0;
    padding-right: 78px;
  }
  .working-group-details > summary {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: flex-end;
    gap: 7.5px;
    position: absolute;
    top: -1.5px;
    right: 0;
    width: fit-content;
    min-width: 33px;
    min-height: 33px;
    margin-left: auto;
    color: var(--accent);
    font: 400 11.25px/1.5 var(--sans);
    cursor: pointer;
    list-style: none;
  }
  .working-group-details > summary::-webkit-details-marker {
    display: none;
  }
  .working-group-details .disclosure-control-icon {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    width: 33px;
    height: 33px;
    font: 400 21px/1 var(--sans);
  }
  .working-group-details .disclosure-control-icon::before {
    content: '+';
  }
  .working-group-details[open] .disclosure-control-icon::before {
    content: '−';
  }
  @media (min-width: 525.75px) and (hover: hover) and (pointer: fine) {
    .working-group-details .disclosure-control-label {
      position: absolute;
      right: calc(100% - 3px);
      top: 50%;
      transform: translateY(-50%);
      font: 400 8.25px/1 var(--sans);
      color: var(--muted);
      white-space: nowrap;
      opacity: 0;
      pointer-events: none;
    }
    .working-group-details > summary:focus-visible .disclosure-control-label {
      right: calc(100% + 7.5px);
    }
    .working-group-details > summary:hover .disclosure-control-label,
    .working-group-details > summary:focus-visible .disclosure-control-label {
      opacity: 1;
    }
  }
  .working-group-details > summary:hover {
    color: var(--ink);
  }
  .working-group-details > :last-child {
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }
  @media print {
    .print-disclosure.working-group-details > h3 {
      display: none;
    }
  }
  .research-publications .papers {
    display: block;
  }
  .research-publications .papers > li {
    min-width: 0;
    margin: 0;
    padding: 15px 12px;
    border-top: 0.75px solid var(--line);
    break-inside: avoid;
  }
  .research-publications .papers > li:last-child {
    border-bottom: 0.75px solid var(--line);
  }
  @media (max-width: 525px) {
    .working-group-onward .section-links.section-links-end {
      align-items: flex-start;
      text-align: left;
    }
    .research-group-cards {
      grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr);
    }
    .research-publications .papers > li {
      padding-inline: 6px;
    }
  }
  @media print {
    .research-group-cards,
    .research-publications .papers {
      display: block;
    }
    .research-group-cards > .working-group + .working-group,
    .research-publications .papers > li + li {
      margin-top: 14pt;
    }
  }
</style>
